<title>USA: Latshaw Enterprises Inc Q4 Nov 2 net, sales rise.</title>
<headline>Latshaw Enterprises Inc Q4 Nov 2 net, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>WICHITA, Kan. 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended    Year Ended</p>
<p>				    Nov 2,   Oct 28,   Nov 2, Oct 28,</p>
<p>				     1996	 1995     1996    1995</p>
<p> Net sales		     $11,392    $9,974  $44,407 $41,102</p>
<p> Income before taxes	     952	 231    2,933   2,134</p>
<p> Income tax provision	    261	  98	994     805</p>
<p> Net income			  691	 133    1,939   1,329</p>
<p>Net income per common and common</p>
<p>equivalent share:</p>
<p>   Primary			 66.83     12.91   187.92  128.80</p>
<p>   Fully Diluted		 35.81	8.41   102.43   72.72</p>
<p>Common and common equivalent</p>
<p>shares outstanding:</p>
<p>   Primary			10,340    10,302   10,318  10,318</p>
<p>   Fully Diluted		20,360    20,330   20,404  20,324</p>
<p>(in thousands except per-share data, statement unaudited)</p>
<p>NOTE: Per share results give retroactive effect to a one-for-50 reverse stock split approved by Latshaw shareholders on December 14, 1996.</p>
<p>		((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
